course: dictionary
lesson: 6109
title: Names with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Michael is a name, and a name is a proper noun. Proper nouns always start with a capital letter, whether they name a person, a place or a day. «Michael Collins circled above the Moon while two friends landed on it.» Michael is a person's name here, so it starts with a capital M.
explain: Many people are called Michael, so the words around the name tell you which one is meant. «Michael Phelps won 28 Olympic medals» is about a swimmer, while «Michael Jackson's album Thriller» is about a singer. Read the context to find out who is being talked about.
explain: Michael also appears in church and Bible stories. In Christian belief, Saint Michael the Archangel leads God's angels against evil, and he is often shown with a sword, defeating a dragon. Michaelmas is his feast day in the church year, so the capital letter shows you a name, not an ordinary word.
fact: Michael is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: Michael is a common boy's and man's name in English-speaking countries.
fact: Short forms of Michael include Mike, Mick, Mikey and Mickey.
fact: In the Bible, Michael is an archangel who leads God's angels against evil.
fact: «Michaelmas» is the church feast day linked to Saint Michael.
exercise: «On 20 July 1969 the American astronauts landed on the Moon while Michael Collins circled above.» Which word is a proper noun for a person? | Moon | Apollo | *Michael | circled
exercise: Mike, Mick and Mikey are all short forms of which name? | *Michael | Michelle | Mitchell
exercise: Which sentence uses capital letters correctly? | michael is a common name. | Michael is a common name. | *Michael is a common name, and it has a capital M.
test: «Saint Michael is shown with a sword, defeating a dragon.» What is Saint Michael shown doing? | Singing in a choir | Swimming in a pool | Baking bread | *Defeating a dragon
test: Which sentence uses capital letters correctly? | *Michael Phelps won 28 Olympic medals. | michael phelps won 28 Olympic medals. | Michael phelps won 28 Olympic medals.
exam: «Michael Phelps won 28 Olympic medals, 23 of them gold.» How many of his medals were not gold? | 28 | *5 | 23 | 3
